## Naming Conventions & Documentation Standards

### Folder Naming
- All **lowercase**, words separated by **hyphens**: `admin-login/`, `employee-list/`, `hiring-pipeline/`
- Each page folder contains exactly 3 files named identically to the folder:
  ```
  admin-login/
  ├── admin-login.html
  ├── admin-login.css
  └── admin-login.js
  ```

### HTML Conventions
- Semantic HTML5 elements: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`
- All interactive elements have unique `id` attributes: `id="btn-submit-login"`, `id="input-email"`
- ID naming: `{element-type}-{purpose}-{context}` → `btn-save-employee`, `input-search-vacancy`, `modal-confirm-delete`
- ARIA labels on all interactive elements for accessibility
- CSS linked via `<link rel="stylesheet">` in `<head>` — **never inline**
- JS linked via `<script src="">` at end of `<body>` — **never inline**
- Each HTML file links: global CSS → component CSS → page CSS → global JS → page JS

### CSS Conventions (BEM Methodology)
- **Block**: `.card`, `.sidebar`, `.navbar`, `.kpi-card`, `.timeline`
- **Element**: `.card__title`, `.card__body`, `.sidebar__link`, `.kpi-card__value`
- **Modifier**: `.card--active`, `.btn--primary`, `.btn--danger`, `.badge--teaching`
- CSS custom properties (variables) defined in `global.css`:
  ```css
  :root {
    --color-primary: #0F1B2D;
    --color-accent: #D4A843;
    /* ... */
  }
  ```
- Class naming: lowercase, hyphen-separated, BEM for components
- No `!important` unless absolutely necessary (documented if used)
- Media queries at bottom of each page CSS file

### JS Conventions
- **Module pattern**: each page JS file is an IIFE or uses `DOMContentLoaded`
- Function naming: `camelCase` — `handleLoginSubmit()`, `fetchEmployees()`, `renderVacancyCards()`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` — `API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB`
- DOM selectors: cached at top of file with `const` — `const btnSubmit = document.getElementById('btn-submit-login')`
- Every function has a JSDoc comment:
  ```js
  /**
   * Fetches employee list from API and renders table rows.
   * @param {number} page - Page number for pagination
   * @param {string} search - Search query string
   * @returns {Promise<void>}
   */
  async function fetchEmployees(page = 1, search = '') { ... }
  ```
- API calls use `fetch()` with async/await — no jQuery, no Axios
- Error handling: try/catch on all API calls with user-facing toast messages

